import ir "sngl:internal/ir"

// Marks the struct that declares a target's build-option schema: the fields an
// `output(...)` block may name.
//
// The mark, not the declaration's name, is what the compiler finds a target's
// options by, so a target may call the struct whatever it likes and a struct
// incidentally named `Options` is not one.
func options() ir.Macro

// Marks what a name nobody declared resolves to. `pattern` is an RE2 regular
// expression, matched against the whole name.
//
// On a component, a name in its package's namespace that matches resolves to
// it. A package whose members cannot be enumerated says so here once — the
// web's element set is open, because a custom element is a tag nobody
// declared — instead of a plugin accepting every identifier silently and
// leaving the compiler nothing to check a call against.
//
// `into` names the prop the matched name binds to, and is what makes the name
// readable: a component resolved by a name nobody declared has no other way to
// learn which one it was. Only a component's mark takes it.
//
// On a component prop, a prop name that matches is accepted at a call site and
// its value checked against the prop's value type. Such a prop is a
// `map<string, V>` and collects every name it matched, keyed by that name —
// one call site binds a wildcard prop as many times as it likes, which a
// scalar has no room for.
//
// A declared name always beats a wildcard, and a name two wildcards match is
// an error rather than whichever was written first.
func wildcard(pattern string, into string = "") ir.Macro

// Marks the const that carries a target's own identity: the value `PLATFORM`
// or `LANGUAGE` is compared against to gate code on the build target.
//
// The compiler supplies the type, which is why the mark exists — the const is
// named for the type it has (`platform`, `language`), so the declaration
// cannot annotate itself without naming the type it is shadowing. The value is
// the target's identifier, written out.
//
// A target's package carries one of these, generated by the loader rather than
// written by hand: a plugin says what it is called by registering under that
// name, and the file the checker mounts into its package says the same thing
// in SNGL, so nothing else has to special-case where the const came from.
func identity() ir.Macro
